Creator: Minh
1. What this website is: Auctions and Peer-to-Peer (P2P) marketplaces are digital platforms connecting buyers and sellers directly. While P2P sites often feature fixed prices, auction marketplaces use competitive bidding to determine the final sale price. Both models empower individuals to monetize items or services directly, cutting out traditional middlemen.
2. How it uses the data files in data: For this website, we will use WebShop data stored at " /scratch/general/vast/u1653932/data_sources/webshop/". WebShop provides only product and price data, so you will have to adapt this into auction data. For auctioning data, this is somewhat dynamic, seller can be emulate with a cheap gpt api endpoint (remember to keep config), the auctioning price progression should follow a script. We probably don't need to use too many products for this.
3. What real world websites it should be modeled after: Ebay
4. Whether the domain has temporal/dynamic data (and how it should simulate): this domain is relatively dynamic
5. Any domain-specific behavior or constraints: no